-**One copy, the frames'.** Shiki and Temml are built once, with the frame runtime (`dist/frames/`): the frames load them, and so does a host-mode page, from `highlight.js` and `math.js` where the host serves the frame documents (`base`), which share their chunks with the runtime. So the host's own bundle has neither, and a page and its frames load the same files, which the browser caches once. In host mode every view of the page shares one highlighter, so Shiki is made once and each grammar loads once, however many views the page opens: one each made the page pay for each grammar again in every view, which in WebKit blocked for seconds over a list of short code blocks ([the spike](https://github.com/comp-markdown/compmd/blob/main/spikes/highlight-perf/README.md)). A host that renders a page itself with `createPage` and gives it `shikiHighlight()` or `temmlMath()` bundles its own; one that renders many pages makes one `shikiHighlight()` and gives it to them all. A host's page with a content security policy allows scripts from where the frames are served. A library the sandbox comes to load next is added the same way: [libraries in the sandbox](https://github.com/comp-markdown/compmd/blob/main/docs/libraries-in-the-sandbox.md) has the steps.
