 **What it costs.** Measured on the frame documents' build (`dist/frames/chunks/`, gzipped at level 9), of what a host serves: Shiki's core is 34.6 KB, its JavaScript engine 19.6 KB, the two themes 4.9 KB, and the 63 grammars 406 KB, about 465 KB in all. A page loads the core, the engine, the themes and the grammars of its blocks: about 75 KB for one with a JavaScript block. Oniguruma is 2.5 KB and its WebAssembly 230 KB, which a page that runs it loads instead of the JavaScript engine. Most grammars are 1 to 15 KB; the largest are C++ (52.9 KB), PHP (27.9 KB), Objective-C (22.7 KB), JSX, TSX, JavaScript and TypeScript (about 16 KB each, each with what it embeds).
 
